    "Postoperative bradycardia and conduction disorders can occur after cardiac surgery, with risks dependent on surgery type and anatomical relationships to the conduction system. Specific guidelines suggest when pacing is recommended, especially after isolated coronary artery bypass surgery. Recommendations include permanent pacing for new postoperative SND or atrioventricular block with persistent symptoms or instability, and temporary pacing wires for coronary artery bypass surgery.": {},
